rows.abstract:
Proposes for the following provisions: 
1) Registration of Social Media Accounts (presentation of valid government-issued ID/valid passport for aliens; parents´ or guardians´ documents and consent for minor media account user);
2) Confidentiality Clause (in accordance with the Data Privacy Act of 2012; written consent of the media account user in case of disclosure to unauthorized persons);
3) Disclosure of Information (. . . the account was or is being used in the commission of a crime or that it was utilized as a means to commit malicious, fraudulent or unlawful act, etc.); 
4) Punishable Acts (personal online account or website containing false information; fictitious online account or website; deceiving content online in the guise of providing one´s service; financing activity employing false content online; etc.);
5) Counteractive Measures (authorizes the Office of Cybercrime of the DOJ to issue order to restrain the commission of the above-mentioned offenses)
Other related terms:  fake news; false/misleading information; fictitious identities; deceiving content; infodemic
